{
  "format_version": 1,
  "id": "diagnosis-01-upgrade-will-not-fix-the-batch",
  "kind": "diagnosis",
  "title": "Will 24 vCores bring the night batch back inside its window?",
  "split": "public",
  "source": "case-exam-v1:1",
  "tags": [
    "capacity",
    "log-rate",
    "upgrade-decision"
  ],
  "prompt": [
    "Client: Harbourline Commerce, a multi-tenant retail order platform with about 400 tenants. Database hlc-orders-prod: Azure SQL Database, Business Critical, Gen5, 16 vCores, compatibility level 160, READ_COMMITTED_SNAPSHOT ON. All times are UTC. Business hours are 07:30 to 18:00. The nightly batch must finish by 06:00. Evidence was collected from Mon 21 Sep to Sun 27 Sep 2026.",
    "The CTO writes: 'Our nightly batch used to finish by about 04:30. Since early September it overruns into business",
    "hours, sometimes until after 09:00. CPU shows 100% in the portal. Our plan is to scale from 16 to 24 vCores this",
    "Friday, about 50% more on the compute line. Please confirm that this is the right move.' The client's comparison of",
    "the two sizes, from the Azure documentation: 16 vCores has 81.6 GB memory, a maximum log rate of 96 MiB/s and 1,680",
    "workers; 24 vCores has 122.4 GB memory, a maximum log rate of 96 MiB/s and 2,520 workers. Name the root cause of the",
    "batch overrun."
  ],
